    {
      "id": "key-text",
      "shape": "text",
      "role": "label",
      "face": "body",
      "text": "Refinement of chapter 3’s final-outcome step for start-session.\nBlue: steps to decide the outcome. Grey: outcomes.\nRavel attempts applicable cleanup before it reports an outcome.\nThis order expresses precedence, not the implementation’s call order.\nOriginal failures keep their status when later cleanup also fails.\nCancellation suppresses a sent result and retains other diagnostics.\nGreen: the only success route. An empty result is a valid value.\nA later nonzero child exit does not invalidate that value.\nA failed final write can leave a prefix. A late signal can interrupt it.\nThe table covers end-session, help and version invocations. This view does not.",
      "x": 389.892578125,
      "y": 800.87734375,
      "anchor": "center",
      "align": "center",
      "wrapped": false,
      "w": 558.2705078125,
      "h": 175.6671875
    }
